eReview` `Pass`/`Fail` also require both jsonl paths. [S1] - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC004 `Other` requires `otherNotes` with at least one non-whitespace character (rejected otherwise with `review_other_notes_required`); scores, `reasons`, `reviewer`, `reviewedAt`, and receipt paths are optional. [S1] - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC005 `otherNotes` with text is rejected unless status is `Other`. [S1] - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC006 Scores lie in [0,1]; `reviewer` <= 256 chars; paths <= 2048 chars; `reviewedAt` needs an explicit offset and is stored UTC; reason items are non-empty. Each violation returns exactly one code from the wire-contract error list, identical on REST, MCP, client, REPL, and both plugin cores (golden contract). The field-to-code map is: `reviewer` over 256 characters or a receipt path over 2048 characters gives `review_field_too_long` naming the field and limit; `reviewedAt` without an explicit offset or not a valid ISO-8601 instant gives `review_timestamp_invalid`; an empty or whitespace-only reason item gives `review_reason_blank`; each is asserted with the same code and HTTP 400 by the golden contract in C#, Pester, and jest (`GoldenContract_FieldToCodeMap_AllSurfaces`). [S1] - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-003-AC007 Validation runs before any mutation on every surface. [S4 +S5 +S6] FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-004 Lossless decimal scores. - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-004-AC001 `0.1234567890123456789` and `0.1234567890123456789012345678` round-trip unchanged through every hop: client JSON [S2], SQLite/PostgreSQL/SQL Server storage [S3], REST and MCP [S5], REPL YAML quoted/unquoted and JsonElement [S6], PowerShell plugin YAML block/flow and JSON [S8], Node core and TypeScript hosts [S9]. - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-004-AC002 A JSON number or numeric string is accepted when its raw text matches `^[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?$` (no sign, no exponent) with a value in [0,1]; a normalized number (trailing fractional zeros stripped) is returned. [S1 +S2] - FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-004-AC003