New AC: TEST-MCP-SESSIONLOG-003-AC001 ClaudeCode completion with class and terminal reviews but no evidence items is accepted; without class it is rejected by the completion gate [S10]. - FR-SUPPORT-014 (FR:2651), TR-SUPPORT-CORE-014 (TR:3809), TEST-SUPPORT-014 (TEST:1532). Changes: complete/fail lifecycle operations run the completion gate; the review write path goes through UpsertTurnAsync (TR ac-4 single point of truth). New ACs: FR `ac-4` complete/fail enforce the completion gate [S10]; TR `ac-5` record review uses UpsertTurnAsync [S4]; TEST `ac-5` complete without class returns 400 [S10]. - FR-MCP-SESSIONLOGSAN-001 (FR:2142, `ac-1`). Changes: the redacted field list adds requestClass and both review records (otherNotes, reasons, reviewer, requestJsonlPath, responseJsonlPath). New AC: `ac-6` review text fields are redacted on every read surface [S4]. - TR-MCP-DTO-001 (TR:924) \"Extended Session Log Entry Fields\". Changes: the turn DTO field list adds requestClass, agentReview, hostileReview; marker prompt session-logging instructions require classification, self-review, and turn closure. New ACs: TR-MCP-DTO-001-AC001 DTO fields present on server and client [S2]; -AC002 marker prompt instructions updated [S11]. - FR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001 (FR:1268), TR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001 (TR:661), TEST-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001 (TEST:612). Changes: \"finalizing the open turn\" becomes \"finalizing every open request turn\", and completeTurn there satisfies the completion gate. New ACs: TR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001-AC001 clear-session completes every open turn whose completion gate and model-evidence check (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005-AC002) are met and leaves any other in progress, reported by requestId with its missing items, never failing it or fabricating reviews [S8]; TEST-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001-AC001 skill text lists the gate steps [S11]. Related, unchanged (no edits; listed so reviewers can check): FR/TR/TEST-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-004 (replay of a `skipped_terminal` record must delete the failsafe, covered by A5 tests); FR-MCP-SESSIONLOGCTX-001 and TR/TEST-MCP-SESSIONLOG-006 (planFile/todoId; pattern reused); FR-SUPPORT-015 / TR-SUPPORT-CORE-015 (additive merge; reviews replace whole records, documented as a single-valued section, not a collection); FR-SUPPORT-012, TR-MCP-SESSIONLOG-001/002/005; TR-MCP-SESSIONLOGSAN-001/002; FR-MCP-TRIAGEPLUGIN-001 (strengthened, no edit); FR-MCP-REPL-009, TR-MCP-REPL-010; TR-MCP-PLUGININT-001, TEST-MCP-PLUGININT-001 (generic outcome catalog gains skipped_terminal through FR-MCP-PLUGININT-001); TR-MCP-CLIENT-001 (new client body types registered); TR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-002 (`Mcp:SessionLog` options section that hosts ReviewThresholds); FR-MCP-HOSTILEREVIEW-001..006 (separate subsystem; the turn `hostileReview` record is distinct and links by requestId); FR-MCP-143 (historical text); FR-MCP-USECASE-003/006/010 (coverage); TR-MCP-DB-006 (review section delete runs under the per-session lock). Pre-existing drift noted, not fixed here: FR-SUPPORT-013 `ac-3` and TEST-SUPPORT-010C-3 / TEST-SUPPORT-022 still describe PUT as 405 (triage). ### Use cases (new, 9) UC-1 Log each user request as exactly one turn. Actors: Operator, agent host (any of the nine), plugin hooks or tools, model. Precondition: workspace trusted (marker signature and health nonce verified). Basic flow: operator submits a prompt; on a prompt-hook or adapter host the hook classifies it as a user request, takes the turn-open lock, derives the nonce from the event (host binding table), asks the server to mint the requestId (the server opens the turn), and records the token as the host session's write target at once; on a bridge host (claude-code, claude-cowork) the arrival bridge mints from the transcript `enqueue` record (state `queued`) and the request becomes the write target at its `dequeue`, or at an `absorbed_mid_turn` removal (FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001-AC009, -AC010); the request enters the stop ledger when it is delivered (at once on prompt-hook and adapter hosts; at its `dequeue` or `absorbed_mid_turn` removal on bridge hosts), never at mint; every verb the model invokes is bound automatically to the host session's write target at invocation start; model closes the turn. Alternate flows: the mint call is retried or replayed and returns the same requestId; a doubly registered hook delivers the event twice and both deliveries get the same requestId (only on hosts whose nonce is a stable per-message id or the bridge's single ordered source; on copilot and classic cline a second registration is refused before any mint, and a second new equal-field invocation fails the host session closed under the equal-field rule, while a stored mint retry or failsafe drain reuses its nonce); the server is unreachable and a provisional `pending-<nonce>` turn is rebound on drain; an identical prompt sent again later is a new event and opens a second turn; background event is skipped (on a bridge host it keeps its queue position as an unminted system entry, so its `dequeue` delivers nothing); operator sends a message mid-turn, the arrival bridge mints its turn at enqueue without touching the running turn or the write target, the message is delivered (absorbed into the running turn, or dequeued) and from then on, while the earlier request is still open, an unqualified write is refused with `request_ambiguous` (D9) and the model names the requestId of each write; once the earlier request is closed, unqualified writes bind to the delivered request; the operator pulls a queued message back (`popAll`) before delivery, the request is withdrawn, and the stop gate asks the model to fail it; a verb without a host session key in a workspace with two live sessions is refused rather than guessed; a subagent's hooks fire and leave this session's turns unchanged; while two delivered requests are open an unqualified verb is refused with `request_ambiguous` and the model names the requestId (D9); on Copilot with more than one MCP prompt hook registered the hook reports `turn_logging_unsupported` and mints nothing (D11); on a host with no arrival mechanism every session-log verb reports `turn_logging_unsupported` (D6). Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001, -002, -003, -007, -008; updated FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-001, FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-002, FR-MCP-REPL-010, FR-MCP-TRIAGESTORE-001. UC-2 Persist session-log writes with truthful receipts. Actors: model, plugin, server. Basic flow: model calls a verb; plugin persists; server returns per-turn outcome; plugin reports persisted only for created/merged. Alternate: target turn is terminal, server reports `skipped_terminal`, plugin reports `persisted:false`, exits non-zero, clears the failsafe; legacy server without outcomes yields `outcomeVerified:false`. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-004; updated FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-003, FR-MCP-PLUGININT-001. UC-3 Close every request turn before stopping. Actors: model, host Stop hook. Basic flow: model records actions/decisions (incl. via `designDecisions`) and closes each turn; Stop hook finds all closed with evidence and passes, clearing the ledger. Alternate: a turn is open (including one whose close the plugin refused for missing model evidence) or fails the completion gate, the Stop hook blocks with the reason and the accepted remedy; a turn closed without evidence by another surface is only warned and never closes turns itself. Alternate: the host session failed closed under D6 (`unsupportedSince`) while a turn was open; the Stop hook blocks with the usual remedy, the model's evidence and close for that turn are captured in the plugin failsafe (reviews are refused and recorded after the drain through the original pair), the next Stop warns instead of blocking, and the next SessionStart drains the captured records with the turn's original pair through the trusted recovery flow. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-005, -006; updated FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-005, FR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001. UC-4 Classify a request. Actors: model. Basic flow: model sets `requestClass` (Code, Docs, Chore) on its turn; an `Unstarted` hostile record flips to Unnecessary for Chore (and back if the class changes away while it is still Unnecessary), on in-progress turns only; records past Unstarted are never changed automatically. Alternate: invalid value rejected. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-001, FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-006. UC-5 Complete or fail a turn under the completion gate. Actors: model, server, server-internal writers. Basic flow: model completes; gate checks class and review statuses; turn completes. Alternate: gate unmet, 400 with missing items, turn stays in progress; fail requires only class; exempt origins bypass; the plugin pre-check refuses locally with the exact gate message; `canceled` is not gated. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONCLASS-002, -003, -004; updated FR-SUPPORT-013, FR-SUPPORT-014. UC-6 Record an agent self-review. Actors: model via any of the nine plugins (on a host recorded `turn_logging_unsupported` every verb reports that code and no review is recorded). Basic flow: model records `agentReview` (Running, then scores); server derives Pass/Fail from thresholds and stamps them. Alternate: conflicting supplied status 422; invalid fields 400; review recorded after completion. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-001, -002, -003, -006, -008, FR-SUPPORT-016 (new); updated FR-MCP-SESSIONLOGSAN-001. UC-7 Record a hostile validation review with receipts. Actors: hostile reviewer (Codex CLI, gpt-6-sol, xhigh), coordinator agent. Basic flow: at the end of each slice once its gates are green, and at P0's end (D10), the coordinator writes the HV brief and launches the Codex reviewer; the runner records the request and response jsonl; the reviewer writes its markdown and JSON receipts; the coordinator records `hostileReview` from the receipt (accuracy/completeness mapped, receipt paths set). Alternate: DISAGREE with passing scores recorded as Other with notes; missing receipt paths rejected; a run whose live model or effort is not gpt-6-sol/xhigh is not accepted as HV; Code or Docs turns of the slice that completed before its HV carry `Other` \"pending slice HV <gate>\" and receive the slice verdict through `recordReview`, each addressed by its original (`sessionId`, `requestId`) pair (FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002-AC002). Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-002, -005. UC-8 Configure review pass thresholds. Actors: operator. Basic flow: operator sets thresholds per kind and score (or per instance); startup and ValidateConfig accept them; new reviews derive with them and stamp them. Alternate: value outside [0,1] rejected. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-007. UC-9 Read review scores losslessly. Actors: agents, client apps. Basic flow: a client reads a turn through REST, MCP, client, REPL, or a plugin and gets the exact decimal scores. Realizes FR-MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-004. ## TDD AC allocation by phase Two kinds of AC. Baseline-green ACs document behavior that exists and passes today; this plan has exactly five (FR-SUPPORT-016 `ac-1`..`ac-4` and TR-SUPPORT-CORE-016 `ac-1`); they need a green receipt from the existing named tests run in P0 (`dotnet test tests/QBrainAi.Support.Mcp.Tests -c Debug --filter \"FullyQualifiedName~SessionLogServiceReplaceDeleteTests\"`, zero failures, zero skips), no RED, and must stay green at every later gate. Every other AC is new or changed behavior and is assigned to the slice that writes its RED test first; extension slices add the same AC on their surface. Per slice, all listed new or changed ACs must be RED before code, mocks-green before production code, and green at the slice gate; the phase HV verifies every new or changed AC of the phase has its RED and green receipts and every baseline-green AC its green receipts. - P0 (no product tests): creates every requirement, AC, mapping, and use case; AC allocation itself is a P0 HV claim. - Phase A   - A1: SESSIONTURN-004-001, -003; SESSIONTURN-001-001..003 (server mint).   - A2: SESSIONTURN-001-006, -007.   - A3: SESSIONTURN-001-001..004, -008, -009, -010